-- title:
--   Generation of the level p² function field by j and j_{p²}
-- statement:
--   For a prime $p$, the predicate `FunctionFieldGeneration` holds at level $M = p\cdot p$. Unfolding the definition, this asserts: for every natural number $d$ dividing $p^2$ and nonzero, the Laurent series $\mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathtt{jq}$ lies in the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\mathtt{jq},\ \mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ (p\cdot p)\ \mathtt{jq})$ of $\mathbb{Q}$-subextensions of the field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, namely the `IntermediateField.adjoin` of the two-element set $\{\mathtt{jq}, \mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ (p\cdot p)\ \mathtt{jq}\}$. Here `jq` is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, and for $N \neq 0$ the map $\mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ N$ is the ring homomorphism of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ obtained by embedding the exponent domain along multiplication by $N$ on $\mathbb{Z}$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$; thus $\mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathtt{jq}$ is $j(q^d)$. Since the divisors of $p^2$ are $1$, $p$ and $p^2$, the content of the assertion is that $j(q^p)$ lies in $\mathbb{Q}\bigl(j(q), j(q^{p^2})\bigr)$, the other two cases being immediate.
--
--   This is the statement that the field generated by all $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid p^2$, coincides with $\mathbb{Q}(j, j_{p^2})$, the formal $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_0(p^2)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the construction of level $p^2\cdot m$ modular polynomial data, being cited by [`ModularCurve.exists_polynomial_eval2_inclusion_eq_of_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_sq_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_polynomial_eval2_inclusion_eq_of_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_sq_mul) and its variants for $p = 2$ and $p = 3$.
